{
  "title": "15: Al-Hijr الحجر",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالۤرٰ تِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْكِتٰبِ وَقُرْاٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(1)\nALIF LAAAM RAA, TILKA AAYAATUL KETAABE WA QUR-AANIM MOBEEN.\nAlif, Lam, Ra. These are the signs of the Book and a manifest Quran.\nرُبَمَا يَوَدُّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَوْ كَانُوْا مُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(2)\nROBAMAA YAWADDUL LAZEENA KAFAROO LAW KAANOO MUSLEMEEN.\nMuch will the faithless wish that they had been Muslims.\nذَرْهُمْ يَاْكُلُوْا وَيَتَمَتَّعُوْا وَيُلْهِهِمُ الْاَمَلُ فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(3)\nZARHUM YAAKOLOO WA YATAMATTA-O’O WA YULHEHEMUL AMALO FASAWFA YA’LAMOON.\nLeave them to eat and enjoy and to be diverted by longings. Soon they will know.\nوَمَاۤ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَرْيَةٍ اِلَّا وَلَهَا كِتَابٌ مَّعْلُوْمٌ‏(4)\nWA MAA AHLAKNAA MIN QARYATIN ILLAA WA LAHAA KETAABUM MA’LOOM.\nWe did not destroy any town but that it had a known term.\nمَا تَسْبِقُ مِنْ اُمَّةٍ اَجَلَهَا وَمَا يَسْتَاْخِرُوْنَ‏(5)\nMAA TASBEQO MIN UMMATIN AJALAHAA WA MAA YASTAAKHEROON.\nNo nation can advance its time nor can it defer it.\nوَ قَالُوْا يٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِىْ نُزِّلَ عَلَيْهِ الذِّكْرُ اِنَّكَ لَمَجْنُوْنٌؕ‏(6)\nWA QAALOO YAA AYYOHAL LAZEE NUZZELA A’LAYHIZ ZIKRO INNAKA LA-MAJNOON.\nThey said, ‘O you, to whom the Reminder has been sent down, you are indeed crazy.\nلَوْ مَا تَاْتِيْنَا بِالْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(7)\nLAW MAA TAATEENAA BIL-MALAAA-EKATE IN KUNTA MENAS SAADEQEEN.\nWhy do you not bring us the angels should you be truthful?!’\nمَا نُنَزِّلُ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةَ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ وَمَا كَانُوْۤا اِذًا مُّنْظَرِيْنَ‏(8)\nMAA NONAZZELUL MALAAA-EKATA ILLAA BIL-HAQQE WA MAA KAANOO EZAM MUNZAREEN.\nWe do not send down the angels except with due reason, and then they will not be granted any respite.\nاِنَّا نَحْنُ نَزَّلْنَا الذِّكْرَ وَاِنَّا لَهٗ لَحٰفِظُوْنَ‏(9)\nINNAA NAHNO NAZZALNAZ ZIKRA WA INNAA LAHU LA-HAAFEZOON.\nIndeed We have sent down the Reminder, and indeed We will preserve it.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِكَ فِىْ شِيَعِ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(10)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA MIN QABLEKA FEE SHEYA-I’L AWWALEEN.\nCertainly We sent [apostles] before you to former communities,\nوَمَا يَاْتِيْهِمْ مِّنْ رَّسُوْلٍ اِلَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(11)\nWA MAA YAATEEHIM MIR RASOOLIN ILLAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZE-OON.\nand there did not come to them any apostle but that they used to deride him.\nكَذٰلِكَ نَسْلُكُهٗ فِىْ قُلُوْبِ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَۙ‏(12)\nKAZAALEKA NASLOKOHU FEE QOLOOBIL MUJREMEEN.\nThat is how We let it pass through the hearts of the guilty:\nلَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖۚ وَقَدْ خَلَتْ سُنَّةُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(13)\nLAA YOAMENOONA BEH, WA QAD KHALAT SUNNATUL AWWALEEN.\nthey do not believe in it, and the precedent of the ancients has already passed.\nوَلَوْ فَتَحْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ بَابًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ فَظَلُّوْا فِيْهِ يَعْرُجُوْنَۙ‏(14)\nWA LAW FATAHNAA A’LAYHIM BAABAM MENAS SAMAAA-E FA-ZALLOO FEEHE YA’ROJOON.\nWere We to open for them a gate of the sky, so that they could go on ascending through it,\nلَقَالُوْۤا اِنَّمَا سُكِّرَتْ اَبْصَارُنَا بَلْ نَحْنُ قَوْمٌ مَّسْحُوْرُوْنَ‏(15)\nLAQAALOO INNAMAA SUKKERAT ABSAARONAA BAL NAHNO QAWMUM MASHOOROON.\nthey would surely say, ‘Indeed a spell has been cast on our eyes; indeed, we are a bewitched lot.’\nوَلَقَدْ جَعَلْنَا فِى السَّمَآءِ بُرُوْجًا وَّزَيَّنّٰهَا لِلنّٰظِرِيْنَۙ‏(16)\nWA LAQAD JA-A’LNAA FIS SAMAAA-E BOROOJANW WA ZAYYANNAAHAA LIN-NAAZEREEN.\nCertainly We have appointed houses in the sky and adorned them for the onlookers,\nوَحَفِظْنٰهَا مِنْ كُلِّ شَيْطٰنٍ رَّجِيْمٍۙ‏(17)\nWA HAFIZNAAHAA MIN KULLE SHAYTAANIR RAJEEM.\nand We have guarded them from every outcast Satan,\nاِلَّا مَنِ اسْتَرَقَ السَّمْعَ فَاَ تْبَعَهٗ شِهَابٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(18)\nILLAA MANIS TARAQAS SAM-A’ FA-ATBA-A’HU SHEHAABUM MOBEEN.\nexcept someone who may eavesdrop, whereat there pursues him a manifest flame.\nوَالْاَرْضَ مَدَدْنٰهَا وَاَلْقَيْنَا فِيْهَا رَوَاسِىَ وَاَنْۢبَتْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ مَّوْزُوْنٍ‏(19)\nWAL ARZA MADADNAAHAA WA ALQAYNAA FEEHAA RAWAASEYA WA AMBATNAA FEEHAA MIN KULLE SHAY-IM MAWZOON.\nAnd We spread out the earth, and cast in it firm mountains, and We grew in it every kind of balanced thing,\nوَجَعَلْنَا لَكُمْ فِيْهَا مَعَايِشَ وَمَنْ لَّسْتُمْ لَهٗ بِرٰزِقِيْنَ‏(20)\nWA JA-A’LNAA LAKUM FEEHAA MA-A’AYESHA WA MAL LASTUM LAHU BE-RAAZEQEEN.\nand made in it [various] means of livelihood for you and for those whom you do not provide for.\nوَاِنْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ اِلَّا عِنْدَنَا خَزَآئِنُهٗ وَمَا نُنَزِّلُهٗۤ اِلَّا بِقَدَرٍ مَّعْلُوْمٍ‏(21)\nWA IM MIN SHAY-IN ILLAA I’NDANAA KHAZAAA-ENOH, WA MAA NONAZZELOHU ILLAA BE-QADARIM MA’LOOM.\nThere is not a thing but that its sources are with Us, and We do not send it down except in a known measure.\nوَاَرْسَلْنَا الرِّيٰحَ لَوَاقِحَ فَاَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَاَسْقَيْنٰكُمُوْهُۚ وَمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ لَهٗ بِخٰزِنِيْنَ‏(22)\nWA ARSALNAR REYAAHA LAWAAQEHA FA-ANZALNAA MENAS SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FA-ASQAYNAAKOMOOH, WA MAA ANTUM LAHU BE-KHAAZENEEN.\nAnd We send the fertilizing winds and send down water from the sky providing it for you to drink and you are not maintainers of its resources.\nوَ اِنَّا لَنَحْنُ نُحْىٖ وَنُمِيْتُ وَنَحْنُ الْوٰرِثُوْنَ‏(23)\nWA INNAA LANAHNO NOHYEE WA NOMEETO WA NAHNUL WAARESOON.\nIndeed it is We who give life and bring death and We are the inheritors.\nوَلَقَدْ عَلِمْنَا الْمُسْتَقْدِمِيْنَ مِنْكُمْ وَلَقَدْ عَلِمْنَا الْمُسْتَاْخِرِيْنَ‏(24)\nWA LAQAD A’LIMNAL MUSTAQDEMEENA MINKUM WA LAQAD A’LIMNAL MUSTAAKHEREEN.\nCertainly We know the predecessors among you and certainly We know the successors,\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ يَحْشُرُهُمْؕ اِنَّهٗ حَكِيْمٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(25)\nWA INNA RABBAKA HOWA YAHSHOROHUM, INNAHU HAKEEMUN A’LEEM.\nand indeed it is your Lord who will resurrect them. Indeed, He is all-wise, all-knowing.\nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ مِنْ صَلْصَالٍ مِّنْ حَمَاٍ مَّسْنُوْنٍۚ‏(26)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAL INSAANA MIN SALSAALIM MIN HAMA-EIM MASNOON.\nCertainly We created man out of a dry clay [drawn] from an aging mud,\nوَالْجَآنَّ خَلَقْنٰهُ مِنْ قَبْلُ مِنْ نَّارِ السَّمُوْمِ‏(27)\nWAL JAANNA KHALAQNAAHO MIN QABLO MIN NAARIS SAMOOM.\nand We created the jinn earlier, out of a piercing fire.\nوَاِذْ قَالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اِنِّىْ خَالِقٌۢ بَشَرًا مِّنْ صَلْصَالٍ مِّنْ حَمَاٍ مَّسْنُوْنٍ‏(28)\nWA IZ QAALA RABBOKA LIL-MALAAA-EKATE INNEE KHAALEQUM BASHARAM MIN SALSAALIM MIN HAMA-EIM MASNOON.\nWhen your Lord said to the angels, ‘Indeed I am going to create a human out of a dry clay [drawn] from an aging mud.\nفَاِذَا سَوَّيْتُهٗ وَنَفَخْتُ فِيْهِ مِنْ رُّوْحِىْ فَقَعُوْا لَهٗ سٰجِدِيْنَ‏(29)\nFA-EZAA SAWWAYTOHU WA NAFAKHTO FEEHE MIR ROOHEE FA-QA-O’O LAHU SAAJEDEEN.\nSo when I have proportioned him and breathed into him of My spirit, then fall down in prostration before him.’\nفَسَجَدَ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةُ كُلُّهُمْ اَجْمَعُوْنَۙ‏(30)\nFA-SAJADAL MALAAA-EKATO KULLOHUM AJMA-O’ON.\nThereat the angels prostrated, all of them together,\nاِلَّاۤ اِبْلِيْسَؕ اَبٰٓى اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ مَعَ السّٰجِدِيْنَ‏(31)\nILLAA IBLEES, ABAA AN-Y YAKOONA MA-A’S SAAJEDEEN.\nbut not Iblis: he refused to be among those who prostrated.\nقَالَ يٰۤاِبْلِيْسُ مَا لَكَ اَلَّا تَكُوْنَ مَعَ السّٰجِدِيْنَ‏(32)\nQAALA YAA IBLEESO MAA LAKA ALLAA TAKOONA MA-A’S SAAJEDEEN.\nHe said, ‘O Iblis! What kept you from being among those who have prostrated?’\nقَالَ لَمْ اَكُنْ لِّاَسْجُدَ لِبَشَرٍ خَلَقْتَهٗ مِنْ صَلْصَالٍ مِّنْ حَمَاٍ مَّسْنُوْنٍ‏(33)\nQAALA LAM AKUL LE-ASJODA LE-BASHARIN KHALAQTAHU MIN SALSAALIM MIN HAMA-EIM MASNOON.\nSaid he, ‘I will not prostrate before a human whom You have created out of a dry clay [drawn] from an aging mud.’\nقَالَ فَاخْرُجْ مِنْهَا فَاِنَّكَ رَجِيْمٌۙ‏(34)\nQAALA FAKHRUJ MINHAA FA-INNAKA RAJEEM.\nHe said, ‘Begone hence, for you are indeed an outcast,\nوَّاِنَّ عَلَيْكَ اللَّعْنَةَ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الدِّيْنِ‏(35)\nWA INNA A’LAYKAL LA’NATA ELAA YAWMID DEEN.\nand indeed the curse shall lie on you until the Day of Retribution.’\nقَالَ رَبِّ فَاَنْظِرْنِىْۤ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(36)\nQAALA RABBE FA-ANZIRNEE ELAA YAWME YUB-A’SOON.\nHe said, ‘My Lord! Respite me till the day they will be resurrected.’\nقَالَ فَاِنَّكَ مِنَ الْمُنْظَرِيْنَۙ‏(37)\nQAALA FA-INNAKA MENAL MUNZAREEN.\nSaid He, ‘You are indeed among the reprieved\nاِلٰى يَوْمِ الْوَقْتِ الْمَعْلُوْمِ‏(38)\nELAA YAWMIL WAQTIL MA’LOOM.\nuntil the day of the known time.’\nقَالَ رَبِّ بِمَاۤ اَغْوَيْتَنِىْ لَاُزَيِّنَنَّ لَهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَاُغْوِيَنَّهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(39)\nQAALA RABBE BEMAA AGHWAYTANEE LA-OZAYYENANNA LAHUM FIL ARZE WA LA-UGHWEYANNAHUM AJMA-E’EN.\nHe said, ‘My Lord! As You have consigned me to perversity, I will surely glamorize [evil] for them on the earth, and I will surely pervert them, all\nاِلَّا عِبَادَكَ مِنْهُمُ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(40)\nILLAA E’BAADAKA MINHOMUL MUKHLASEEN.\nexcept Your dedicated servants among them.’\nقَالَ هٰذَا صِرَاطٌ عَلَىَّ مُسْتَقِيْمٌ‏(41)\nQAALA HAAZAA SERAATUN A’LAYYA MUSTAQEEM.\nHe said, ‘This is the path [leading] straight to Me.\nاِنَّ عِبَادِىْ لَيْسَ لَكَ عَلَيْهِمْ سُلْطٰنٌ اِلَّا مَنِ اتَّبَعَكَ مِنَ الْغٰوِيْنَ‏(42)\nINNA E’BAADEE LAYSA LAKA A’LAYHIM SULTAANUN ILLAA MANIT TABA-A’KA MENAL GHAAWEEN.\nIndeed, as for My servants you do not have any authority over them, except the perverse who follow you,\nوَاِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ لَمَوْعِدُهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(43)\nWA INNA JAHANNAMA LA-MAW-E’DOHUM AJMA-E’EN.\nand indeed hell is the tryst of them all.\nلَهَا سَبْعَةُ اَبْوَابٍؕ لِكُلِّ بَابٍ مِّنْهُمْ جُزْءٌ مَّقْسُوْمٌ‏(44)\nLAHAA SAB-A’TO ABWAAB, LE-KULLE BAABIM MINHUM JUZ-UM MAQSOOM.\nIt has seven gates, and to each gate belongs a separate portion of them.’\nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍؕ‏(45)\nINNAL MUTTAQEENA FEE JANNAATINW WA O’YOON.\nIndeed the Godwary will be amid gardens and springs.\nاُدْخُلُوْهَا بِسَلٰمٍ اٰمِنِيْنَ‏(46)\nUDKHOLOOHAA BE-SALAAMIN AAMENEEN.\n‘‘Enter it in peace and safety!’’\nوَنَزَعْنَا مَا فِىْ صُدُوْرِهِمْ مِّنْ غِلٍّ اِخْوَانًا عَلٰى سُرُرٍ مُّتَقٰبِلِيْنَ‏(47)\nWA NAZA’NAA MAA FEE SODOOREHIM MIN GHILLIN IKHWAANAN A’LAA SORORIM MOTAQAABELEEN.\nWe will remove whatever rancour there is in their breasts; [intimate like] brothers, [they will be reclining] on couches, facing one another.\nلَا يَمَسُّهُمْ فِيْهَا نَصَبٌ وَّمَا هُمْ مِّنْهَا بِمُخْرَجِيْنَ‏(48)\nLAA YAMASSOHUM FEEHAA NASABUNW WA MAA HUM MINHAA BE-MUKHRAJEEN.\nTherein neither weariness shall touch them, nor will they [ever] be expelled from it.\nنَبِّئْ عِبَادِىْۤ اَنِّىْۤ اَنَا الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُۙ‏(49)\nNABBEA E’BAADEE ANNEE ANAL GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nInform my servants that I am indeed the All-forgiving, the All-merciful,\nوَاَنَّ عَذَابِىْ هُوَ الْعَذَابُ الْاَلِيْمُ‏(50)\nWA ANNA A’ZAABEE HOWAL A’ZAABUL ALEEM.\nand that My punishment is a painful punishment.\nوَنَبِّئْهُمْ عَنْ ضَيْفِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَۘ‏(51)\nWA NABBEAHUM A’N ZAYFE IBRAAHEEM.\nAnd inform them about the guests of Abraham,\nاِذْ دَخَلُوْا عَلَيْهِ فَقَالُوْا سَلٰمًاؕ قَالَ اِنَّا مِنْكُمْ وَجِلُوْنَ‏(52)\nIZ DAKHALOO A’LAYHE FA-QAALOO SALAAMAA, QAALA INNAA MINKUM WAJELOON.\nwhen they entered into his presence and said, ‘Peace!’ He said, ‘We are indeed afraid of you.’\nقَالُوْا لَا تَوْجَلْ اِنَّا نُبَشِّرُكَ بِغُلٰمٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(53)\nQAALOO LAA TAWJAL INNAA NOBASH-SHEROKA BE-GHOLAAMIN A’LEEM.\nThey said, ‘Do not be afraid. Indeed we give you the good news of a wise son.’\nقَالَ اَبَشَّرْتُمُوْنِىْ عَلٰٓى اَنْ مَّسَّنِىَ الْكِبَرُ فَبِمَ تُبَشِّرُوْنَ‏(54)\nQAALA ABASH-SHARTOMOONEE A’LAA AM MASSANEYAL KEBARO FABEMA TOBASH-SHEROON.\nHe said, ‘Do you give me good news though old age has befallen me? What is the good news that you bring me?’\nقَالُوْا بَشَّرْنٰكَ بِالْحَقِّ فَلَا تَكُنْ مِّنَ الْقٰنِطِيْنَ‏(55)\nQAALOO BASH-SHARNAAKA BIL-HAQQE FALAA TAKUM MENAL QAANETEEN.\nThey said, ‘We bring you good news in truth; so do not be despondent.’\nقَالَ وَمَنْ يَّقْنَطُ مِنْ رَّحْمَةِ رَبِّهٖۤ اِلَّا الضَّآلُّوْنَ‏(56)\nQAALA WA MAN-Y YAQNATO MIR RAHMATE RABBEHI ILLAZ ZAALLOON.\nHe said, ‘Who despairs of his Lord’s mercy except the astray?!’\nقَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكُمْ اَيُّهَا الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ‏(57)\nQAALA FAMAA KHATBOKUM AYYOHAL MURSALOON.\nHe said, ‘O messengers, what is now your errand?’\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّاۤ اُرْسِلْنَاۤ اِلٰى قَوْمٍ مُّجْرِمِيْنَۙ‏(58)\nQAALOO INNAA URSILNAA ELAA QAWMIM MUJREMEEN.\nThey said, ‘We have been sent toward a guilty people,\nاِلَّاۤ اٰلَ لُوْطٍؕ اِنَّا لَمُنَجُّوْهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(59)\nILLAA AALA LOOT, INNAA LA-MONAJJOOHUM AJMA-E’EN.\n[who shall perish] except the family of Lot. We will indeed deliver all of them,\nاِلَّا امْرَاَتَهٗ قَدَّرْنَاۤ ۙ اِنَّهَا لَمِنَ الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‏(60)\nILLAM RA-ATAHU QADDARNAA, INNAHAA LAMENAL GHAABEREEN.\nexcept his wife, [who], We have ordained, will indeed be among those who remain behind.’\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ اٰلَ لُوْطِ ۨالْمُرْسَلُوْنَۙ‏(61)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-A AALA LOOTENIL MURSALOON.\nSo when the messengers came to Lot’s family,\nقَالَ اِنَّكُمْ قَوْمٌ مُّنْكَرُوْنَ‏(62)\nQAALA INNAKUM QAWMUM MUNKAROON.\nhe said, ‘You are indeed strangers [to me].’\nقَالُوْا بَلْ جِئْنٰكَ بِمَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَمْتَرُوْنَ‏(63)\nQAALOO BAL JEANAAKA BEMAA KAANOO FEEHE YAMTAROON.\nThey said, ‘Indeed, we bring you what they used to doubt.\nوَ اَتَيْنٰكَ بِالْحَقِّ وَاِنَّا لَصٰدِقُوْنَ‏(64)\nWA ATAYNAAKA BIL-HAQQE WA INNAA LA-SAADEQOON.\nWe bring you the truth, and indeed, we speak truly.\nفَاَسْرِ بِاَهْلِكَ بِقِطْعٍ مِّنَ الَّيْلِ وَاتَّبِعْ اَدْبَارَهُمْ وَلَا يَلْتَفِتْ مِنْكُمْ اَحَدٌ وَّامْضُوْا حَيْثُ تُؤْمَرُوْنَ‏(65)\nFA-ASRE BE-AHLEKA BE-QIT-I’M MENAL LAYLE WAT TABE’ ADBAARAHUM WA LAA YALTAFIT MINKUM AHADUNW WAM ZOO HAYSO TOAMAROON.\nTake your family in a watch of the night; and follow in their rear, and none of you should turn round, and proceed as you are bidden.’\nوَقَضَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِ ذٰ لِكَ الْاَمْرَ اَنَّ دَابِرَ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ مَقْطُوْعٌ مُّصْبِحِيْنَ‏(66)\nWA QAZAYNAA ELAYHE ZAALEKAL AMRA ANNA DAABERA HAA-OLAAA-E MAQTOO-U’M MUSBEHEEN.\nWe apprised him of the matter that these will be rooted out by dawn.\nوَجَآءَ اَهْلُ الْمَدِيْنَةِ يَسْتَبْشِرُوْنَ‏(67)\nWA JAAA-A AHLUL MADEENATE YASTABSHEROON.\nThe people of the city came, rejoicing.\nقَالَ اِنَّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ ضَيْفِىْ فَلَا تَفْضَحُوْنِۙ‏(68)\nQAALA INNA HAA-OLAAA-E ZAYFEE FALAA TAFZAHOON.\nHe said, ‘These are indeed my guests. Do not bring dishonour on me.\nوَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَلَا تُخْزُوْنِ‏(69)\nWAT TAQUL LAAHA WA LAA TUKHZOON.\nBe wary of Allah and do not humiliate me.’\nقَالُوْۤا اَوَلَمْ نَنْهَكَ عَنِ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(70)\nQAALOO AWA LAM NANHAKA A’NIL A’ALAMEEN.\nThey said, ‘Did we not forbid you from [defending ] strangers?’\nقَالَ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ بَنٰتِىْۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ فٰعِلِيْنَؕ‏(71)\nQAALA HAA-OLAAA-E BANAATEE IN KUNTUM FAA-E’LEEN.\nHe said, ‘These are my daughters, [marry them] if you should do anything.’\nلَعَمْرُكَ اِنَّهُمْ لَفِىْ سَكْرَتِهِمْ يَعْمَهُوْنَ‏(72)\nLA-A’MROKA INNAHUM LAFEE SAKRATEHIM YA’MAHOON.\nBy your life, they were bewildered in their drunkenness.\nفَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الصَّيْحَةُ مُشْرِقِيْنَۙ‏(73)\nFA-AKHAZATHOMUS SAYHATO MUSHREQEEN.\nSo the Cry seized them at sunrise,\nفَجَعَلْنَا عَالِيَهَا سَافِلَهَا وَ اَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ حِجَارَةً مِّنْ سِجِّيْلٍؕ‏(74)\nFA-JA-A’LNAA A’ALEYAHAA SAAFELAHAA WA AMTARNAA A’LAYHIM HEJAARATAM MIN SIJJEEL.\nand We made its topmost part its nethermost, and rained on them stones of shale.\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّلْمُتَوَسِّمِيْنَ‏(75)\nINNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAATIL LIL-MOTAWASSEMEEN.\nThere are indeed signs in that for the percipient.\nوَاِنَّهَا لَبِسَبِيْلٍ مُّقِيْمٍ‏(76)\nWA INNAHAA LABE-SABEELIM MOQEEM.\nIndeed it is on a standing road,\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَؕ‏(77)\nINNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYATAL LIL-MOAMENEEN.\nand there is indeed a sign in that for the faithful.\nوَاِنْ كَانَ اَصْحٰبُ الْاَيْكَةِ لَظٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(78)\nWA IN KAANA ASHAABUL AYKATE LA-ZAALEMEEN.\nIndeed the inhabitants of Aykah were [also] wrongdoers.\nفَانتَقَمْنَا مِنْهُمْۘ وَاِنَّهُمَا لَبِاِمَامٍ مُّبِيْنٍؕ‏(79)\nFANTAQAMNAA MINHUM, WA INNAHOMAA LABE-EMAAMIM MOBEEN.\nSo We took vengeance on them, and indeed the two of them are on an open highway.\nوَلَقَدْ كَذَّبَ اَصْحٰبُ الْحِجْرِ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَۙ‏(80)\nWA LAQAD KAZZABA ASHAABUL HIJRIL MURSALEEN.\nCertainly the inhabitants of Hijr denied the apostles.\nوَاٰتَيْنٰهُمْ اٰيٰتِنَا فَكَانُوْا عَنْهَا مُعْرِضِيْنَۙ‏(81)\nWA AATAYNAAHUM AAYAATENAA FA-KAANOO A’NHAA MO’REZEEN.\nWe had given them Our signs but they disregarded them.\nوَكَانُوْا يَنْحِتُوْنَ مِنَ الْجِبَالِ بُيُوْتًا اٰمِنِيْنَ‏(82)\nWA KAANOO YANHETOONA MENAL JEBAALE BOYOOTAN AAMENEEN.\nThey used to hew out dwellings from mountains feeling secure.\nفَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الصَّيْحَةُ مُصْبِحِيْنَۙ‏(83)\nFA-AKHAZATHOMUS SAYHATO MUSBEHEEN.\nSo the Cry seized them at dawn,\nفَمَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَؕ‏(84)\nFAMAA AGHNAA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nand what they used to earn did not avail them.\nوَمَا خَلَقْنَا السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَاۤ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ ؕ وَاِنَّ السَّاعَةَ لَاٰتِيَةٌ فَاصْفَحِ الصَّفْحَ الْجَمِيْلَ‏(85)\nWA MAA KHALAQNAS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA ILLAA BIL-HAQ, WA INNAS SAA-A’TA LA-AATEYATUN FASFAHIS SAFHAL JAMEEL.\nWe did not create the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them except with consummate wisdom, and indeed the Hour is bound to come. So forbear with a graceful forbearance.\nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ الْخَلّٰقُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(86)\nINNA RABBAKA HOWAL KHALLAAQUL A’LEEM.\nIndeed your Lord is the All-creator, the All-knowing.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنٰكَ سَبْعًا مِّنَ الْمَثَانِىْ وَالْقُرْاٰنَ الْعَظِيْمَ‏(87)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAAKA SAB-A’M MENAL MASAANEE WAL QUR-AANAL A’ZEEM.\nCertainly We have given you [the surah of] the seven oft-repeated verses and the great Quran.\nلَا تَمُدَّنَّ عَيْنَيْكَ اِلٰى مَا مَتَّعْنَا بِهٖۤ اَزْوَاجًا مِّنْهُمْ وَلَا تَحْزَنْ عَلَيْهِمْ وَاخْفِضْ جَنَاحَكَ لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(88)\nLAA TAMUDDANNA A’YNAYKA ELAA MAA MATTA’NAA BEHI AZWAAJAM MINHUM WA LAA TAHZAN A’LAYHIM WAKH FIZ JANAAHAKA LIL-MOAMENEEN.\nDo not extend your glance toward what We have provided to certain groups of them, and do not grieve for them, and lower your wing to the faithful,\nوَقُلْ اِنِّىْۤ اَنَا النَّذِيْرُ الْمُبِيْنُۚ‏(89)\nWA QUL INNEE ANAN NAZEERUL MOBEEN.\nand say, ‘I am indeed a manifest warner [of punishment from God],’\nكَمَاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَى الْمُقْتَسِمِيْنَۙ‏(90)\nKAMAA ANZALNAA A’LAL MUQTASEMEEN.\nlike that We sent down upon those who split into bands,\nالَّذِيْنَ جَعَلُوا الْقُرْاٰنَ عِضِيْنَ‏(91)\nLAZEENA JA-A’LUL QUR-AANA E’ZEEN.\nwho represented the Quran as magic.\nفَوَرَبِّكَ لَنَسْئَلَنَّهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(92)\nFAWA RABBEKA LANAS-ALANNAHUM AJMA-E’EN.\nBy your Lord, We will question them all\nعَمَّا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(93)\nA’MMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nconcerning what they used to do.\nفَاصْدَعْ بِمَا تُؤْمَرُ وَ اَعْرِضْ عَنِ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(94)\nFASDA’ BEMAA TOAMARO WA A-A’RIZ A’NIL MUSHREKEEN.\nSo proclaim what you have been commanded, and turn away from the polytheists.\nاِنَّا كَفَيْنٰكَ الْمُسْتَهْزِءِيْنَۙ‏(95)\nINNAA KAFAYNAAKAL MUSTAHZE-EEN.\nIndeed We will suffice you against the deriders\nالَّذِيْنَ يَجْعَلُوْنَ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَۚ فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(96)\nLAZEENA YAJ-A’LOONA MA-A’L LAAHE ELAAHAN AAKHAR, FASAWFA YA’LAMOON.\n—those who set up another deity besides Allah. Soon they will know!\nوَلَقَدْ نَعْلَمُ اَنَّكَ يَضِيْقُ صَدْرُكَ بِمَا يَقُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(97)\nWA LAQAD NA’LAMO ANNAKA YAZEEQO SADROKA BEMAA YAQOOLOON.\nCertainly We know that you become upset because of what they say.\nفَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ وَكُنْ مِّنَ السّٰجِدِيْنَۙ‏(98)\nFA-SABBEH BE-HAMDE RABBEKA WA KUM MENAS SAAJEDEEN.\nSo celebrate the praise of your Lord and be among those who prostrate,\nوَاعْبُدْ رَبَّكَ حَتّٰى يَاْتِيَكَ الْيَقِيْنُ‏(99)\nWA’BUD RABBAKA HATTAA YAATEYAKAL YAQEEN.\nand worship your Lord until certainty comes to you.",
  "merits": "There are 99 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that whoever recites Surah Hijr will get the reward equal to the number of Muhajireen and Ansaar (companions of the Holy Prophet [s.a.w.a.]) and this Surah should be written with saffron and then worn as a talisman by a new mother who cannot produce enough milk for her child.\nIf written and tied on one’s arm, it makes any business conducted by the wearer to be profitable and makes people like doing business with him. His sustenance thus increases. In a narration by Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) one can also put this Surah (written) inside the pocket or safe (for storing valuables)."
}
